compliance, small business attorney advice through our legal plans, compliance concierge, compliance and legal concierge, reinstatement concierge and compliance concierge, business concierge, business and legal concierge, consumer attorney advice through legal plans, business licenses, virtual mail and check deposit services, estate planning bundle, bookkeeping, e-signature, and trademark monitoring. The company was incorporated in 1999 and is headquartered in Mountain View, California.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Jeffrey M. Stibel | CEO & Chairman | Age 51 | Compensation: $1.3M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 1K people. Revenue per employee of $632K ranks in the top quartile among Industrials peers, with revenue growing 7%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $124K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $95K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 2\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (9/10).","financial_summary":["LegalZoom.com, Inc. is a small-cap industrials business with a $793M market cap on $756M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +7% over the past three years, a respectable pace for a business of this size. Operating margins are expanding by +4.5pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Gross margins of 66% are the starting point for assessing pricing power.","The business throws off $148M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 20 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 11.55\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage of 19\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Management returns a meaningful 10.2% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and stock-based comp at 15% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insiders hold 5.2% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.3\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (-0.2) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 9.9% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Significant insider selling (net $3.5M)","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","dollars":-3501526.35},{"text":"Cyclicality and capital intensity \u2014 order books turn on a dime, and the heavy fixed cost base that creates the moat also magnifies the downturn.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Supply chain reshoring costs and labour shortages \u2014 onshoring mandates raise capex requirements while a shrinking skilled-labour pool inflates operating costs.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without warning.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Gross margin tops the Industrials peer set \u2014 genuine pricing power is present here","Among the least levered in Industrials \u2014 the fortress balance sheet in its peer set"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Contrasting LegalZoom.com (NASDAQ:LZ) and TeleTech (NASDAQ:TTEC)","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/13/contrasting-legalzoom-com-nasdaqlz-and-teletech-nasdaqttec.html",